== General Modeling Information

This subsection covers decisions made for the models in this project on the coding side. The `brms` and `emdi` code for fitting the various models can be found at @appendix_code in the appendix. The STAN code generated by `brms` can be found in the appendix as well at @appendix_stan. The models shown there are the intercept only and full models, as those cover the situations with and without additional components. For fitting the bayesian models, each has $10,000$ iterations and $5,000$ iterations for warmup across 4 chains. This gives a total of $20,000$ post-warmup iterations per model. 

Predictions are acquired through the `brms::posterior_epred()` function, which takes draws from the expected value of the posterior predictive distribution. This is an important distinction from pulling from the full posterior predictive distribution, as that incorporates the known sampling variance from the direct estimates. The goal of this project is to better estimate the underlying true vacancy rates $bold(theta)$, not generate new realizations of direct estimates $bold(Y)$. To justify this, because a Gaussian family is used for this model,

$
  E[Y_i | theta_i, sigma_i] = theta_i
$

and the distribution of $theta_i$ is what is being estimated in this project. An explanation of the various prediction methods provided by `brms` is shown in @brms_prediction_explainer created by Andrew Heiss @brmsPredictionsExplainer.

